Description: Spatial Immune Receptor Utilities Package. A consolidated
    toolkit for long-read spatial immune receptor sequencing. SIRUP takes
    demultiplexed reads from the companion 'RRAD' package and runs an
    end-to-end IgBLAST and pRESTO pipeline to produce AIRR-style
    rearrangement tables with spatial IDs and coordinates. It also provides
    Visium HD barcode mapping, clonal summaries, tree plotting, polygon
    annotation, and spatial statistics. If you use SIRUP, please cite Melton
    et al. (bioRxiv), 'SIRUP, a toolkit for spatial B and T cell receptor
    repertoires, reveals differences between normal and ectopic germinal
    centers in myasthenia gravis'. Run citation("SIRUP") for the reference.
